WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:09.992
The next morning Ally was about to put on her meld medallion when Alpha chimed and her screen blinked on.

2
00:00:09.993 --> 00:00:15.589
"Alpha! You're recalibrated!" Ally cheered.

3
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:20.315
"I cannot wait to get my powers back. It's no fun being a human.

4
00:00:20.316 --> 00:00:28.770
I can't read people's minds, and I've broken three plates here at home and lots of dishes at the diner, and I can't count fast or—"

5
00:00:28.771 --> 00:00:33.375
Alpha's screen had strange wavy lines. "Memory overload!

6
00:00:33.376 --> 00:00:38.260
Recalibration incomplete! Corrupted files must be deleted!"

7
00:00:38.261 --> 00:00:41.487
"Oh no." Ally's heart sank.

8
00:00:41.488 --> 00:00:43.731
"How long will that take?"

9
00:00:43.732 --> 00:00:47.992
"Unclear. Commencing shutdown to execute full repairs."

10
00:00:47.993 --> 00:00:51.233
Alpha's screen blinked off and then quickly back on.

11
00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:58.597
"Warning! Do not touch power sources until reboot is complete, or else complete system failure is assured!"

12
00:00:58.598 --> 00:01:05.536
"I won't touch anything until you're back to yourself," Ally said. "I promise."

13
00:01:05.537 --> 00:01:09.797
"Hurry up, Alpha," she thought as she put on her meld medallion.

14
00:01:09.798 --> 00:01:18.999
"Even though you can be really bossy, I miss you. And I need you!"

15
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.410
*** It was a very busy morning at the

16
00:01:23.411 --> 00:01:31.511
diner. "It's like everyone in Sandville showed up for breakfast today," Ally said as she and Flo waited at the kitchen for their customers'

17
00:01:31.512 --> 00:01:35.116
orders. "You can say that again!" Ray

18
00:01:35.117 --> 00:01:38.492
huffed. "Why did I send Randy to work the food truck

19
00:01:38.493 --> 00:01:41.443
today?" "You had no choice," Flo

20
00:01:41.444 --> 00:01:45.707
said. "The truck was booked to serve food at Splash Town

21
00:01:45.708 --> 00:01:48.311
Park." "I know." Ray wiped his

22
00:01:48.312 --> 00:01:52.416
brow. "I just could use his help in the kitchen. Here's your order,

23
00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:56.753
Ally." Ally grabbed the two plates and hurried to deliver them to Phil and

24
00:01:56.754 --> 00:01:59.930
Tina. "Two breakfast

25
00:01:59.931 --> 00:02:03.457
sandwiches!" "Thanks, Ally," Phil

26
00:02:03.458 --> 00:02:08.967
said. While Ally refilled their coffee cups, Tina took a bite of her

27
00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:11.771
sandwich. "You're right, Phil," she

28
00:02:11.772 --> 00:02:16.010
said. "This is the best breakfast sandwich I've ever

29
00:02:16.011 --> 00:02:19.849
had! Say, how's your new computer,

30
00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.778
Ally?" "It's fine, thanks," Ally

31
00:02:22.779 --> 00:02:28.931
said. She wasn't sure why Tina was curious about her new computer, but Ally didn't really want to talk about

32
00:02:28.932 --> 00:02:34.227
it. She couldn't bear to think about what would happen if Alpha couldn't recalibrate

33
00:02:34.228 --> 00:02:38.431
successfully. "How much RAM does it have?" Tina asked

34
00:02:38.432 --> 00:02:42.448
her. "Ram?" Ally repeated. "I,

35
00:02:42.449 --> 00:02:43.206
uh—"

36
00:02:43.207 --> 00:02:48.335
Crash! "Gah!" The sound of pans crashing was followed by Ray

37
00:02:48.336 --> 00:02:53.279
yelling. Ally ran to the kitchen. "Ray! Are you all right?"

38
00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:58.328
"There are too many orders, and I can't keep up!" Ray moaned.

39
00:02:58.329 --> 00:03:01.467
"I've got to get Randy back here."

40
00:03:01.468 --> 00:03:04.454
"He just texted me," Flo said.

41
00:03:04.455 --> 00:03:09.335
"He already has a huge line of customers at the food truck."

42
00:03:09.336 --> 00:03:14.973
"Excuse me." A woman with long purple hair walked up to the counter.

43
00:03:14.974 --> 00:03:18.475
"I couldn't help but overhear that you're short-staffed today.

44
00:03:18.476 --> 00:03:21.275
I'm a chef, passing through town as I head west.

45
00:03:21.276 --> 00:03:23.255
I'd be happy to help you out.

46
00:03:23.256 --> 00:03:29.781
I've already eaten my breakfast, and I was impressed. It was delicious!"

47
00:03:29.782 --> 00:03:34.354
Ray looked at all the orders waiting to be filled.

48
00:03:34.355 --> 00:03:37.351
"Can you work a grill?" he asked hopefully.

49
00:03:37.352 --> 00:03:40.669
"Better than most back east," she replied.

50
00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.279
"What's your name?" Ray asked.

51
00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.835
"Melanie."

52
00:03:44.836 --> 00:03:49.805
"Then come on back to the kitchen, please, Melanie!" Ray said.

53
00:03:49.806 --> 00:03:52.967
Finally, it was the end of the day.

54
00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:58.944
The diner was empty, and Ally, Flo, Ray, and Melanie were having a cold drink.

55
00:03:58.945 --> 00:04:04.878
"Phew! My feet are tired!" Flo flopped down onto a stool.

56
00:04:04.879 --> 00:04:07.684
"So are my hands!" Ray said.

57
00:04:07.685 --> 00:04:11.985
"I can't remember the last time I flipped so many burgers in one day."

58
00:04:11.986 --> 00:04:15.404
"You're a pretty fast flipper," Melanie said.

59
00:04:15.405 --> 00:04:18.482
"You're not bad yourself." Ray smiled.

60
00:04:18.483 --> 00:04:20.111
"Seriously, thank you.

61
00:04:20.112 --> 00:04:23.598
I couldn't have gotten through the day without your help."

62
00:04:23.599 --> 00:04:27.853
"I'm happy to come back tomorrow too if you need help," Melanie said.

63
00:04:27.854 --> 00:04:30.506
"That would be great," Ray said.

64
00:04:30.507 --> 00:04:35.657
"The food truck is booked at a carnival for the next two days, so I'll be without my cook again."

65
00:04:35.658 --> 00:04:40.070
"No worries." Melanie grabbed her backpack from behind the counter.

66
00:04:40.071 --> 00:04:46.950
"I'll see you in the morning."

67
00:04:46.951 --> 00:04:51.109
"What luck," Flo said after Melanie had left.

68
00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:53.273
"She saved the day."

69
00:04:53.274 --> 00:04:55.326
Mateo had just entered.

70
00:04:55.327 --> 00:05:00.016
"Did somebody say 'luck'? I wish I had some."

71
00:05:00.017 --> 00:05:03.090
"What's wrong, Mateo?" Ally asked.

72
00:05:03.091 --> 00:05:07.672
"You look like you lost your best friend," Flo said.

73
00:05:07.673 --> 00:05:12.932
"Well, he did. Bethany is still out of town," Ally said.

74
00:05:12.933 --> 00:05:17.197
"No, it's not that." Mateo sat down.

75
00:05:17.198 --> 00:05:24.482
"Someone calling themselves UserPFM5 keeps outbidding me for the first Cosmic Quest comic.

76
00:05:24.483 --> 00:05:27.579
And the auction ends really soon."

77
00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:32.874
"That's terrible," Ally said. "What can you do about it?"

78
00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:38.914
"Only one thing," Mateo said. "Keep bidding until the bitter end!"

